17.4 Record identity

A proposed record uses exactly one of:
- tempKey for a response-local new proposal;
- targetId for an application-reserved current slot.

A targetId must:
- already exist;
- belong to the same project;
- belong to the correct stage and operation;
- belong to the current scope;
- permit completion or update;
- expose only agent-writable fields.

Humans and agents cannot allocate canonical IDs.

